%N A401620 Sum of products of parts in all partitions of n into relatively prime parts.
%H A401620 Alois P. Heinz, <a href="/A401620/b401620.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%e A401620 a(6) = 25 = 1 + 2 + 4 + 3 + 6 + 4 + 5: 111111, 21111, 2211, 3111, 321, 411, 51.
%e A401620 a(8) = 130 = 1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 3 + 6 + 12 + 9 + 18 + 4 + 8 + 12 + 5 + 10 + 15 + 6 + 7: 11111111, 2111111, 221111, 22211, 311111, 32111, 3221, 3311, 332, 41111, 4211, 431, 5111, 521, 53, 611, 71.
%p A401620 b:= proc(n, i, g) option remember; `if`(n=0 or i=1, `if`(n>0 or g<2, 1, 0),
%p A401620       b(n, i-1, g)+b(n-i, min(n-i, i), igcd(i, g))*i)
%p A401620     end:
%p A401620 a:= n-> b(n$2,0):
%p A401620 seq(a(n), n=0..36);
%Y A401620 Cf. A000837, A006906.
